  "A carbon monoxide alarm means leave now. Warn everyone in the house, go outside, and call 112 from outside. Don't go back in until the emergency services say it's safe. In danger: call 112. Smell gas? Go outside and call your gas network operator's emergency line (on your gas bill and at the meter), or 112.": "Carbon monoxide alarm? Go outside and call 112 from outside.",
  "A carbon monoxide alarm means leave now. Warn everyone in the house, go outside, and from outside call 0800 111 999 (Northern Ireland: 0800 002 001). If anyone feels unwell, call 999. Don't go back in until the emergency services say it's safe.": "Carbon monoxide alarm? Go outside, then call 0800 111 999 (Northern Ireland: 0800 002 001), or 999 if anyone is unwell.",
  "A carbon monoxide alarm means leave now. Warn everyone in the house, go outside, and from outside call 0800 111 999 (Northern Ireland: 0800 002 001). If anyone feels unwell, call 999. Don't go back in until the emergency services say it's safe. In danger: call 999. Smell gas? Go outside and call 0800 111 999 (Northern Ireland: 0800 002 001), free, day and night.": "Carbon monoxide alarm? Go outside, then call 0800 111 999 (Northern Ireland: 0800 002 001), or 999 if anyone is unwell.",
  "Dat is de gastoevoer: handen terug. Was je de ketel aan het bijvullen, draai dan de kraan op de vulslang dicht. Aan gas werkt alleen een CO-vrij gecertificeerd bedrijf. Ruik je gas? Bel 0800-9009.": "Dat is de gastoevoer. Aan gas werkt alleen een CO-vrij gecertificeerd bedrijf. Ruik je gas? 0800-9009.",
