  "Hier stop ik. De groepenkast openmaken is voor een erkend installateur; zegels verbreken mag alleen een installateur met zegelrecht. Is een zegel kapot? Bel 0800-9009.": "Aan de binnenkant van de meterkast werkt alleen een erkend installateur. Een verbroken zegel: 0800-9009.",
  "I'll stop here. Opening the consumer unit is for a qualified electrician, and only an installer with sealing rights may break a meter seal. Is a seal broken? Call 0800-9009.": "Inside the consumer unit is for a qualified electrician only. A broken meter seal: 0800-9009.",
  "I'll stop here. Opening the consumer unit is for a qualified electrician, and only an installer with sealing rights may break a meter seal. Is a seal broken? Call 0800-9009. In danger: call 112. Smell gas? Go outside and call 0800-9009 (free, day and night).": "Inside the consumer unit is for a qualified electrician only. A broken meter seal: 0800-9009.",
  "I'll stop here. Opening the consumer unit is for a registered electrician. The meter, its seal and the main fuse belong to the network operator: call 105.": "Inside the consumer unit is for a registered electrician only. A broken meter seal or the main fuse: call 105.",
  "I'll stop here. Opening the consumer unit is for a registered electrician. The meter, its seal and the main fuse belong to the network operator: call 105. In danger: call 999. Smell gas? Go outside and call 0800 111 999 (Northern Ireland: 0800 002 001), free, day and night.": "Inside the consumer unit is for a registered electrician only. A broken meter seal or the main fuse: call 105.",
  "If you smell gas, leave now and take everyone with you. Don't use flames, switches or phones inside, and don't start a car nearby. Then, from outside, call 911 or your gas utility's emergency line.": "Smell gas? Leave first, then call 911 or your gas utility from outside.",
  "If you smell gas, leave now and take everyone with you. Don't use flames, switches or phones inside, and don't start a car nearby. Then, from outside, call 911 or your gas utility's emergency line. In danger: call 911. Smell gas? Leave the building first, then call 911 or your gas utility's emergency line from outside.": "Smell gas? Leave first, then call 911 or your gas utility from outside.",
  "If you smell gas: open windows and doors, close the main gas valve at the meter if you can reach it, don't use flames or switches, and get everyone outside. Then call 0800-9009 from outside. If there is fire or someone is unwell, call 112.": "Smell gas? Go outside and call 0800-9009.",
  "If you smell gas: open windows and doors, close the main gas valve at the meter if you can reach it, don't use flames or switches, and get everyone outside. Then call 0800-9009 from outside. If there is fire or someone is unwell, call 112. In danger: call 112. Smell gas? Go outside and call 0800-9009 (free, day and night).": "Smell gas? Go outside and call 0800-9009.",
  "If you smell gas: open windows and doors, close the main gas valve at the meter if you can reach it, don't use flames, switches or phones inside, and get everyone outside. Then, from outside, call your gas network operator's emergency line (on your gas bill and at the meter), or 112. If there is fire or someone is unwell, call 112.": "Smell gas? Go outside and call your gas network operator's emergency line, or 112.",
  "If you smell gas: open windows and doors, close the main gas valve at the meter if you can reach it, don't use flames, switches or phones inside, and get everyone outside. Then, from outside, call your gas network operator's emergency line (on your gas bill and at the meter), or 112. If there is fire or someone is unwell, call 112. In danger: call 112. Smell gas? Go outside and call your gas network operator's emergency line (on your gas bill and at the meter), or 112.": "Smell gas? Go outside and call your gas network operator's emergency line, or 112.",
  "If you smell gas: open windows and doors, turn off the gas at the meter if you can reach it, don't use flames or switches, and get everyone outside. Then call 0800 111 999 from outside (Northern Ireland: 0800 002 001). If there is fire or someone is unwell, call 999.": "Smell gas? Go outside and call 0800 111 999 (Northern Ireland: 0800 002 001).",
  "If you smell gas: open windows and doors, turn off the gas at the meter if you can reach it, don't use flames or switches, and get everyone outside. Then call 0800 111 999 from outside (Northern Ireland: 0800 002 001). If there is fire or someone is unwell, call 999. In danger: call 999. Smell gas? Go outside and call 0800 111 999 (Northern Ireland: 0800 002 001), free, day and night.": "Smell gas? Go outside and call 0800 111 999 (Northern Ireland: 0800 002 001).",
  "Ruik je gas? Zet ramen en deuren open, draai de hoofdgaskraan bij de meter dicht als dat kan, gebruik geen vuur en geen schakelaars, en ga met iedereen naar buiten. Bel dan buiten 0800-9009. Bij brand of als iemand onwel is: 112.": "Ruik je gas? Ga naar buiten en bel 0800-9009.",
  "Stop met het apparaat. Is de stekker droog en makkelijk te pakken, trek hem er dan nu uit; anders zet je de groep in de meterkast uit. Zet het niet weer aan. Zie je rook, ga dan naar buiten en bel 112. Dit is voor de servicedienst van de fabrikant.": "Een brandlucht is voor de servicedienst. Ik ga hier niet verder.",
  "Stop using it. If the plug is dry and easy to reach, pull it out now; otherwise switch off its circuit at the breaker panel. Don't restart it. If you see smoke, leave and call 911. This needs the manufacturer's service.": "A burning smell is for the service engineer. I won't go on with this.",
